# T-152-007 Execution Plan

## Goal
READ-ONLY smoke audit of 8 MCP lifecycle tools via stdio JSON-RPC:
deckent_init, deckent_set_directives, deckent_plan, deckent_start,
deckent_status, deckent_review, deckent_retro, deckent_cleanup.

## Steps
1. Read src/mcp/ server implementation to understand:
   - Tool registration (tools/list handler)
   - Input schemas (Zod)
   - Tool handlers (destructive vs readonly)
2. Start MCP stdio server (node dist/mcp/... or npx deckent mcp)
3. Send JSON-RPC requests:
   - initialize
   - tools/list (inventory check)
   - tools/call for each lifecycle tool (read-only parameters only,
     dry-run / missing args to avoid side-effects)
4. For each tool evaluate:
   - Listed in tools/list? (PASS/MISSING)
   - Schema sound? (PASS/DRIFT)
   - Returns markdown or JSON as expected? (PASS/FAIL)
   - Zod validation blocks bad input? (PASS/FAIL)
   - Destructive behaviour gated? (PASS/CONCERN)
5. Write findings to docs/audits/sprint-152/T-152-007-mcp-lifecycle.md
6. Write .result

## Scope discipline
- Only file written under src/: NONE
- Only file written under tests/: NONE
- Report-only: docs/audits/sprint-152/T-152-007-mcp-lifecycle.md
- Do NOT call deckent_kill, deckent_cleanup with real args,
  deckent_start with real args — schema check only.

## Done criteria
- Report exists with 8 lifecycle tools × findings
- Evidence: tools/list raw snippet, tools/call sample outputs
- Sprint 153+ action items list
- 0 source/test diff
